<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
   What the system may take a copy of, on Android 11 and older.

   Everything the app keeps is worth restoring onto a new phone — the tasks,
   the measurements, the media library — so this says what must NOT go rather
   than what may.

   corrupt_state holds verbatim copies of payloads this app could not read.
   They exist so that a parsing bug cannot destroy anything, which is a
   question about this device and this install; carrying them to a new phone
   restores nothing and can be several megabytes of it.

   The covers stay out of the cloud copy because of the quota. Auto-backup
   stops at 25 MB per app, and a media library of three hundred covers reaches
   that on its own — at which point the system gives up on the whole backup,
   tasks included, and says nothing. A cover can be picked again; a year of
   tasks cannot. The app's own export does carry the covers.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="file" path="corrupt_state" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="media_covers" />
</full-backup-content>
